{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-23123","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23548","text":"The Three-Protocol Stack: [&], PULSE, PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-23124","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23549","text":"This document explains how the three [&] ecosystem protocols compose into a complete substrate for accountable, evolvable, benchmarkable agent systems."}]},{"id":"blk-23125","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM    — measures loops over time      (diagnostic)   │ OS-009\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE    — declares loops + circulation   (temporal)    │ OS-010\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&]      — composes capabilities          (structural)  │ AmpersandBoxDesign\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-23126","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23550","text":"What each layer answers"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23128","spans":[{"id":"spn-23551","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-23129","spans":[{"id":"spn-23552","text":"Question"}]},{"id":"blk-23130","spans":[{"id":"spn-23553","text":"Artifact"}]}],"id":"blk-23127","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23131","spans":[{"id":"spn-23554","text":"[[&]](../../AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/index.md)"}]},{"id":"blk-23132","spans":[{"id":"spn-23555","text":"What can each agent do, and how do they compose?"}]},{"id":"blk-23133","spans":[{"id":"spn-23556","marks":["code"],"text":"*.ampersand.json"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23134","spans":[{"id":"spn-23557","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-23135","spans":[{"id":"spn-23558","text":"How do their processes cycle and signal each other?"}]},{"id":"blk-23136","spans":[{"id":"spn-23559","marks":["code"],"text":"*.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-23560","text":" (loop manifest)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23137","spans":[{"id":"spn-23561","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-23138","spans":[{"id":"spn-23562","text":"How well do those cycles actually work over time?"}]},{"id":"blk-23139","spans":[{"id":"spn-23563","text":"Diagnostic reports + leaderboards"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23140","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23564","text":"A customer adopting all three writes (at minimum) two files:"}]},{"id":"blk-23141","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"acme-insurance/\n├── acme.ampersand.json   # [&] — capability declarations\n└── acme.pulse.json       # PULSE — loop topology + cadence + connections"},{"id":"blk-23142","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23565","text":"PRISM does not require a separate file — it reads the PULSE manifest directly to discover phases, signatures, and substrates."}]},{"id":"blk-23143","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23566","text":"Three closed loops, three nesting levels"}]},{"id":"blk-23144","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23567","text":"The reference [&] ecosystem already operates with three nested loops:"}]},{"id":"blk-23145","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"PRISM (outer)        compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose\n  │\n  └─ Graphonomous    retrieve → route → act → learn → consolidate\n       │\n       └─ Deliberation    survey → triage → dispatch → act → learn"},{"id":"blk-23146","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23568","text":"PULSE encodes this nesting in the "},{"id":"spn-23569","marks":["code"],"text":"nesting"},{"id":"spn-23570","text":" block of each manifest:"}]},{"id":"blk-23147","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23149","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23571","marks":["code"],"text":"prism.benchmark"},{"id":"spn-23572","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-23573","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.continual_learning]"}]}],"id":"blk-23148","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23151","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23574","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.continual_learning"},{"id":"spn-23575","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-23576","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.deliberate]"}]}],"id":"blk-23150","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23153","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23577","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-23578","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-23579","marks":["code"],"text":"parent_loop: graphonomous.continual_learning"}]}],"id":"blk-23152","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23154","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23580","text":"OS-008 (Agent Harness, draft) is expected to add a fourth outer layer. PULSE supports unbounded nesting depth — adding OS-008 is just another manifest with "},{"id":"spn-23581","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [prism.benchmark]"},{"id":"spn-23582","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-23155","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23583","text":"How signals flow"}]},{"id":"blk-23156","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23584","text":"Cross-loop signals carry one of five canonical tokens through CloudEvents-compatible envelopes:"}]},{"id":"blk-23157","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"                              ┌────────────────────┐\n                              │  ReputationUpdate  │ ────────────────┐\n                              └────────────────────┘                  │\n                                       ▲                              ▼\n                                       │                    ┌──────────────────┐\n                              ┌────────┴────────┐           │ fleetprompt.trust │\n                              │ OutcomeSignal   │           │  (marketplace)    │\n                              └────────┬────────┘           └──────────────────┘\n                                       │\n        ┌──────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┐\n        │                              │                            │\n        ▼                              ▼                            ▼\n┌──────────────┐            ┌──────────────────┐         ┌────────────────────┐\n│ graphonomous │ ──signal──▶│  prism.benchmark │         │ agentromatic.delib │\n│ (memory loop)│            │ (eval loop)      │         │ (consensus loop)   │\n└──────┬───────┘            └────────┬─────────┘         └─────────┬──────────┘\n       │                             │                              │\n       │ TopologyContext             │ DeliberationResult           │\n       ▼                             ▼                              ▼\n┌──────────────┐            ┌──────────────────┐         ┌────────────────────┐\n│ ConsolidationEvent          (read by other loops as substrate state)        │\n└──────────────┘            └──────────────────┘         └────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-23158","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23585","text":"The five tokens are stable for v0.1:"}]},{"id":"blk-23159","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23161","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23586","marks":["code"],"text":"TopologyContext"},{"id":"spn-23587","text":" — emitted by "},{"id":"spn-23588","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-23589","text":", consumed by "},{"id":"spn-23590","marks":["code"],"text":"route"}]}],"id":"blk-23160","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23163","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23591","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationResult"},{"id":"spn-23592","text":" — emitted by inner deliberation loops"}]}],"id":"blk-23162","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23165","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23593","marks":["code"],"text":"OutcomeSignal"},{"id":"spn-23594","text":" — emitted by "},{"id":"spn-23595","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-23596","text":" after action results"}]}],"id":"blk-23164","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23167","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23597","marks":["code"],"text":"ReputationUpdate"},{"id":"spn-23598","text":" — canonical reputation/confidence delta"}]}],"id":"blk-23166","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23169","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23599","marks":["code"],"text":"ConsolidationEvent"},{"id":"spn-23600","text":" — emitted by "},{"id":"spn-23601","marks":["code"],"text":"consolidate"},{"id":"spn-23602","text":" phases"}]}],"id":"blk-23168","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-23170","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23603","text":"Conformance composition"}]},{"id":"blk-23171","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23604","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-23605","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-23606","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-23607","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-23608","text":" and its runtime passes all 12 conformance tests."}]},{"id":"blk-23172","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23609","text":"A system is "},{"id":"spn-23610","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-23611","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-23612","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-23613","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-23614","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-23615","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-23616","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-23617","text":" phase."}]},{"id":"blk-23173","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23618","text":"A system is "},{"id":"spn-23619","marks":["bold"],"text":"[&]-composable"},{"id":"spn-23620","text":" if its agents declare capabilities with matching "},{"id":"spn-23621","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-23622","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-23623","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-23624","text":" contracts."}]},{"id":"blk-23174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23625","text":"The three layers are independent. A system may adopt one without the others. Adoption order is typically:"}]},{"id":"blk-23175","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23626","marks":["bold"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-23627","text":" (capability declarations) — earliest, lowest commitment"}]}],"id":"blk-23176","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23179","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23628","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE"},{"id":"spn-23629","text":" (loop manifest) — when the system has closed feedback"}]}],"id":"blk-23178","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23630","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM"},{"id":"spn-23631","text":" (benchmarking) — when the loop is ready to be measured"}]}],"id":"blk-23180","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-23182","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23632","text":"Why three protocols, not one"}]},{"id":"blk-23183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23633","text":"A monolithic protocol covering capabilities, loops, and benchmarking would be larger, harder to evolve, and harder to adopt incrementally. The three-layer split mirrors how HTTP, HTML, and CSS became ubiquitous separately before converging in the browser."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23185","spans":[{"id":"spn-23634","text":"Concern"}]},{"id":"blk-23186","spans":[{"id":"spn-23635","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-23187","spans":[{"id":"spn-23636","text":"Cadence of change"}]}],"id":"blk-23184","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23188","spans":[{"id":"spn-23637","text":"What can be done"}]},{"id":"blk-23189","spans":[{"id":"spn-23638","text":"[&]"}]},{"id":"blk-23190","spans":[{"id":"spn-23639","text":"months–years"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23191","spans":[{"id":"spn-23640","text":"How it cycles"}]},{"id":"blk-23192","spans":[{"id":"spn-23641","text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-23193","spans":[{"id":"spn-23642","text":"weeks–months"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23194","spans":[{"id":"spn-23643","text":"How well it works"}]},{"id":"blk-23195","spans":[{"id":"spn-23644","text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-23196","spans":[{"id":"spn-23645","text":"continuous"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23646","text":"Different rates of change deserve different protocols."}]},{"id":"blk-23198","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23647","text":"Related"}]},{"id":"blk-23199","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23201","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23648","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-23649","text":" — how every product fits the stack"}]}],"id":"blk-23200","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23203","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23650","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"},{"id":"spn-23651","text":" — versions, test counts, deployment state"}]}],"id":"blk-23202","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23652","text":"[[&] Protocol docs](../../AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/index.md) — capability composition (structural)"}]}],"id":"blk-23204","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23653","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"OS-010 PULSE specification"},{"id":"spn-23654","text":" — loop + circulation algebra (temporal)"}]}],"id":"blk-23206","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23209","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23655","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"OS-009 PRISM specification"},{"id":"spn-23656","text":" — cross-system benchmark (diagnostic)"}]}],"id":"blk-23208","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23211","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23657","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/graphonomous/docs/spec/README.md"}],"text":"Graphonomous spec"},{"id":"spn-23658","text":" — the reference memory loop these protocols compose around"}]}],"id":"blk-23210","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23212","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23659","text":"PULSE implementation docs"}]},{"id":"blk-23213","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23215","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23660","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/ARITHMETIC_INTEGRATION.md"}],"text":"Arithmetic Integration"},{"id":"spn-23661","text":" — how PULSE phases gate on the box-and-box kernel verdict"}]}],"id":"blk-23214","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23217","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23662","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/V0.2-BEHAVIORAL-TYPES.md"}],"text":"V0.2 Behavioral Types"},{"id":"spn-23663","text":" — session-typed phase contracts (draft)"}]}],"id":"blk-23216","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23664","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/V0.2-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md"}],"text":"V0.2 Implementation Plan"},{"id":"spn-23665","text":" — roadmap for the v0.2 manifest schema"}]}],"id":"blk-23218","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23666","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/NPM_PACKAGE.md"}],"text":"NPM Package"},{"id":"spn-23667","text":" — the PULSE validator/conformance package"}]}],"id":"blk-23220","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierah6g4yyycxhvgmwqwd375oyn2pc7x5ciogb63w4yc33arzpu3ccba","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}